+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn, so the caller still receives the rejection, `onError` fires with the session and the thrown error, and `afterSession` fires after it ([validated by: runs onError with the session and the thrown error, and still rejects the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L37), [validated by: runs afterSession after onError](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L65)). Because the failure lands before the turn did anything, an `afterSession` hook must tolerate a session whose entries are exactly what the caller supplied: no user input was read or rewritten, no model response was produced, and nothing was streamed or executed.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
